{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Named Entity Recognition Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: BIO tagging helpers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def spans_to_bio(tokens, spans):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    labels = [\"O\"] * len(tokens)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for start, end, label in spans:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        labels[start] = f\"B-{label}\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(start + 1, end):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            labels[i] = f\"I-{label}\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return labels"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def bio_to_spans(tokens, labels):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    spans = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    current = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i, label in enumerate(labels):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if label.startswith(\"B-\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if current:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                spans.append(current)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            current = (i, i + 1, label[2:])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        elif label.startswith(\"I-\") and current and current[2] == label[2:]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            current = (current[0], i + 1, current[2])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if current:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                spans.append(current)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                current = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if current:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        spans.append(current)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return spans"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> tokens = [\"Apple\", \"sued\", \"Google\", \"over\", \"iPhone\", \"sales\", \".\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> labels = [\"B-ORG\", \"O\", \"B-ORG\", \"O\", \"B-PRODUCT\", \"O\", \"O\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ">>> bio_to_spans(tokens, labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "[(0, 1, 'ORG'), (2, 3, 'ORG'), (4, 5, 'PRODUCT')]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: hand-crafted features"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For classical (non-neural) NER, features are the game. Useful ones:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def token_features(token, prev_token, next_token):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"lower\": token.lower(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"is_upper\": token.isupper(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"is_title\": token.istitle(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"has_digit\": any(c.isdigit() for c in token),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"suffix_3\": token[-3:].lower(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"shape\": word_shape(token),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"prev_lower\": prev_token.lower() if prev_token else \"<BOS>\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"next_lower\": next_token.lower() if next_token else \"<EOS>\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def word_shape(word):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for c in word:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if c.isupper():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            out.append(\"X\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        elif c.islower():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            out.append(\"x\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        elif c.isdigit():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            out.append(\"d\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            out.append(c)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return \"\".join(out)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`word_shape(\"iPhone\")` returns `xXxxxx`. `word_shape(\"USA-2024\")` returns `XXX-dddd`. Capitalization patterns are high-signal for proper nouns."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: a simple rule-based + dictionary baseline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ORG_GAZETTEER = {\"Apple\", \"Google\", \"Microsoft\", \"OpenAI\", \"Meta\", \"Amazon\", \"Netflix\"}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "GPE_GAZETTEER = {\"US\", \"USA\", \"UK\", \"India\", \"Germany\", \"France\"}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "PRODUCT_GAZETTEER = {\"iPhone\", \"Android\", \"Windows\", \"ChatGPT\", \"Claude\"}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def rule_based_ner(tokens):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    labels = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for token in tokens:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if token in ORG_GAZETTEER:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            labels.append(\"B-ORG\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        elif token in GPE_GAZETTEER:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            labels.append(\"B-GPE\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        elif token in PRODUCT_GAZETTEER:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            labels.append(\"B-PRODUCT\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            labels.append(\"O\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return labels"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Production gazetteers have millions of entries scraped from Wikipedia and DBpedia. Coverage is good. Disambiguation (`Apple` the company vs the fruit) is terrible. That is why statistical models won."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: the CRF step (sketch, not full impl)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Full CRF from scratch in 50 lines is not enlightening without the probability-theory foundations. Use `sklearn-crfsuite` instead:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import sklearn_crfsuite"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def to_features(tokens):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i, tok in enumerate(tokens):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        prev = tokens[i - 1] if i > 0 else \"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        nxt = tokens[i + 1] if i + 1 < len(tokens) else \"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out.append({"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"word.lower()\": tok.lower(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"word.isupper()\": tok.isupper(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"word.istitle()\": tok.istitle(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"word.isdigit()\": tok.isdigit(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"word.suffix3\": tok[-3:].lower(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"word.shape\": word_shape(tok),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"prev.word.lower()\": prev.lower(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"next.word.lower()\": nxt.lower(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"BOS\": i == 0,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"EOS\": i == len(tokens) - 1,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        })"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "crf = sklearn_crfsuite.CRF(algorithm=\"lbfgs\", c1=0.1, c2=0.1, max_iterations=100, all_possible_transitions=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "X_train = [to_features(s) for s in sentences_tokenized]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "crf.fit(X_train, bio_labels_train)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`c1` and `c2` are L1 and L2 regularization. `all_possible_transitions=True` lets the model learn illegal sequences (e.g., `I-ORG` after `O`) are unlikely, which is how a CRF enforces BIO consistency without you writing the constraint."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: what a BiLSTM-CRF adds"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Features become learned. Inputs: token embeddings (GloVe or fastText). LSTM reads left-to-right and right-to-left. Concatenated hidden states go through a CRF output layer. The CRF still enforces tag-sequence consistency; the LSTM replaces hand-crafted features with learned ones."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class BiLSTM_CRF_Head(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, vocab_size, embed_dim, hidden_dim, n_labels):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.embed = nn.Embedding(vocab_size, embed_dim)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.lstm = nn.LSTM(embed_dim, hidden_dim, bidirectional=True, batch_first=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.fc = nn.Linear(hidden_dim * 2, n_labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, token_ids):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        e = self.embed(token_ids)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h, _ = self.lstm(e)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        emissions = self.fc(h)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return emissions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For the CRF layer, use `torchcrf.CRF` (pip install pytorch-crf). The gain over hand-crafted CRF is measurable but smaller than you expect unless you have tens of thousands of labeled sentences."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Implement `bio_to_spans` (the inverse of `spans_to_bio`) and verify round-trip consistency on 10 sentences.\n2. **Medium.** Train the sklearn-crfsuite CRF above on the CoNLL-2003 English NER dataset. Report per-entity F1 using `seqeval`. Typical result: ~84 F1.\n3. **Hard.** Fine-tune `distilbert-base-cased` on a domain-specific NER dataset (medical, legal, or financial). Compare against the spaCy small model. Document data leakage checks and write up what surprised you."
      ]
    }
